.TH WERKMEISTER-MACHINE-DETECT 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-machine\-detect \- Generate \e<repo>/.werkmeister/services.yaml from the repo's package manifests, Dockerfiles, compose, Helm and k8s files (re\-runs only add what is missing)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister machine detect\fR [repo]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the report and the proposed YAML; write nothing
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
Write without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-assist\fR
Ask Claude to resolve the fields the scan had to guess
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assist\fR
Never ask Claude
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
It reads \fBpackage.json\fR and workspaces (npm, pnpm, yarn), Dockerfiles, docker\-compose files, Helm charts (rendered with \fBhelm template\fR), raw k8s manifests and kustomize overlays (\fBkubectl kustomize\fR). For each value the report shows where it came from, and every guess is marked. Guesses are written with a \fB# guessed:\fR comment, so they're easy to find and fix.
.PP
\fBport_offset\fR is picked from the offsets no other repo under \fBpaths.repos_root\fR uses. The shared install service's \fBnode_modules_volume\fR is named \fB<repo>\-node\-modules\fR, and with a lockfile its command never rewrites the lockfile (for pnpm, \fBpnpm install \-\-frozen\-lockfile\fR). Infrastructure (redis, postgres and other datastores) gets the next free \fBk8s_forward_port\fR from 9050.
.PP
Re\-running only adds services and keys the file doesn't have yet. Nothing already in the file changes: not values, comments or formatting. After writing, run \fBwerkmeister registry sync\fR.
.PP
\fB\-\-assist\fR runs one read\-only Claude session (Read, Glob and Grep only) over the repo. It only answers the listed questions: a non\-Node service's dev command, health path, environment, secrets, \fBdepends_on\fR, and which service an unmatched Deployment belongs to. Answers are written with \fB# inferred by Claude:\fR and never replace a value the scan read from a file.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
